Subject: [PATCH 02/37] tools/aurora-sep: add sleep-drain-probe.py

s2idle on J414s wakes the whole SoC about 3.7 times per second of sleep
(per-CPU s2idle entry counts), and the source is not a wakeup source.
The probe snapshots the battery energy, the time suspended
(CLOCK_BOOTTIME - CLOCK_MONOTONIC), each CPU's s2idle entries,
/proc/interrupts and, as root, the wakeup sources, and reports the drain
in W, wakes per suspended second and the interrupts that fired, between
two snapshots or around one systemctl suspend. It only reads, except
that 'around' asks systemd to suspend.

